# Historic Structure Report, Part I, J. Slyder Farm Buildings (National Park Service, Gettysburg NMP, historical data of December 11, 1958 by Historian Frederick Tilberg; architectural data of 1959)
# Second reading (workstream bt-web, 2026-11-15): the report was read to the end (PDF pp. 9-12 and 15 carry its content; pp. 1-8 are memoranda and title sheets; pp. 13, 14 and 16 are photographs).
# PDF pp. 9, 10 and 11 were looked at as page images. The text layer of PDF p. 11 (Architectural Data) is a damaged OCR (a for e: 'Tha housa'); its quotes are typed in cleaned form and every wrong letter is a {{saved|fixed}} pair.
# The report is a park study of 1958-59 about buildings as they stood then; each statement below is dated by what the report says about the part (pre-war = standing in July 1863; post-war = later).
